Subject: New tool: STIG Multi-Checklist Editor — what it does better than STIG Viewer

Team,

I've been building an offline, single-file HTML tool for working with multiple .cklb checklists at once, styled after STIG Viewer 3 but with a bunch of things STIG Viewer either can't do or makes painful. Wanted to give you a rundown before we start using it.

No install needed — it's one HTML file, runs entirely in your browser, nothing leaves your machine, no server or account required. Open it, drop in your .cklb files, done.

WORKING ACROSS MULTIPLE CHECKLISTS AT ONCE
- Every checklist opens in its own tab, plus an "All checklists" tab that aggregates everything — no more opening one .cklb at a time.
- Compare tab: line up the same STIG across several devices/checklists side by side and see exactly which rules differ, with a toggle to show only the differences.
- Fill Checklists: fill out one checklist as a "master" and push its answers into every other checklist that shares the same Vuln IDs — huge time-saver when the same STIG applies to a fleet of identical systems. Can also spin up a blank checklist from an existing one's structure to use as that master.
- Copy to other checklists: copy one rule's (or a whole selection's) status/comments/finding details over to its matching rule in any other open checklist.

OVERVIEW / REPORTING
- Overview tab aggregates stats across any set of checklists: overall status donut, CAT I/II/III severity breakdowns, an "Open Findings by STIG" drill-down (STIG → open Vuln ID → which devices have it open → their comments/finding details), a per-checklist score table, and STIG coverage.
- New: Total/Open tables per unique Vuln ID, broken out by CAT I, CAT II, and CAT III — so you can see, e.g., "8 unique CAT I checks, 4 of them open somewhere" at a glance instead of digging through each device.
- Overview exports to a print-ready HTML or PDF report (light or dark theme) — a real report, not just a screenshot.
- New: "Export Findings (CSV)" — a flattened, one-row-per-finding spreadsheet (STIG, Vuln ID, severity, status, comments, finding details, classification, CCIs, severity override info) for feeding into a POA&M, tracker, or eMASS upload. STIG Viewer doesn't give you anything like this without third-party tools.

SEARCH AND BULK EDITING
- Real search syntax: commas/spaces = OR, quotes = exact phrase, capitalized AND to require both, scoped to specific fields (title, check text, fix text, discussion, comments) or all of them, with matches highlighted right in the list.
- Multi-select rules (shift/ctrl-click) and bulk-set status, or bulk append/replace comments and finding details across many rules at once — instead of clicking into each one.
- Hover a row and hit N/O/X/R to set its status without even clicking into it; works on a whole multi-selection at once too.

SEVERITY OVERRIDE AND CLASSIFICATION
- Severity Override with required justification, same as STIG Viewer — except here the override actually takes effect everywhere severity matters (CAT filter tabs, Overview stats, Compare), not just as a label on one screen.
- Classification marking (None/Unclassified/CUI/FOUO) settable independently on Target Data, Comments, and Finding Details, plus a one-click "Apply to All Checks" button that stamps the same marking across every check in a checklist plus its Target Data in one shot — instead of setting it rule by rule.

IMPORT
- Import a .cklb's findings into an already-open checklist (matched by STIG + Vuln ID), with a "skip already-modified rules" safeguard.
- New: Import XCCDF/SCC scan results (.xml) directly — it maps automated pass/fail/N/A results onto the matching Vuln IDs, pulls host data (hostname, IP, MAC, role) into Target Data, and deliberately leaves manual/OCIL questions alone for us to review by hand rather than guessing at them.

QUALITY OF LIFE
- Autosave straight back to the original file (Chrome/Edge, via the File System Access API) — no repeated export/re-import cycle.
- Duplicate-file detection when loading, so you can't accidentally open the same checklist twice.
- "Export Tool + Checklists" — hand someone a single self-contained file with checklists already loaded in it, optionally locked read-only, so they don't need to import anything themselves.
- Role and Technology Area fields are now proper dropdowns matching STIG Viewer's actual option lists, instead of free text.

Happy to walk anyone through it or take requests for anything else that'd help our workflow.

